Bill bakes 300 rolls, 120 chocolate croissants, and 60 baguettes every day. Each roll is 4 inches long, so they are 300 * 4 = 1200 inches long. Each croissant is 6 inches long, so they are 120 * 6 = 720 inches long. Each baguette is two feet long, so they are 60 * 12 = 720 inches long. Bill puts all the baked goods end to end, so they are 1200 + 720 + 720 = 2640 inches long. 2640 inches is 22 feet.

{id 155}: {"answers": {"155": 22}}

